1454..1527 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1528..1585 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1586..1657 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1658..1734 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1735..1811 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1812..1886 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
1887..1965 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
1966..2008 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
